# OpenStreetMap sign-in (optional).
#
# Everything the app does by default -- running queries, geocoding place names,
# tag autocompletion, exporting -- works with no account and no key. This one
# setting only enables the account extras: showing who you are, saving queries
# to your OSM preferences, and filing a map note from a result.
#
# Leave it unset and the sign-in button simply does not appear.
#
# To get a client id:
#   1. https://www.openstreetmap.org/oauth2/applications -> Register new application
#   2. Leave "Confidential application?" UNCHECKED. This is a browser app, so it
#      uses PKCE and has no secret to protect. If OSM shows you a secret, the
#      box is still ticked.
#   3. Redirect URIs, one per line:
#        http://127.0.0.1:5173/oauth-callback.html
#        https://<your-user>.github.io/<your-repo>/oauth-callback.html
#      Only 127.0.0.1 may use http; everything else must be https.
#   4. Permissions: read_prefs, write_prefs, write_notes. Nothing else.
#
# The client id is public by design: it ships inside the JavaScript bundle.
# Copy this file to .env.local for development. For a GitHub Pages deploy, set
# it as a repository variable named VITE_OSM_CLIENT_ID instead.

VITE_OSM_CLIENT_ID=
